Implemented M11d as a shared cross-app lifecycle contract, reusing the existing event layer.

**Contract** (`twenty-shared/cross-app-events`): stable names `<family>.<action>` over families `document/task/calendarEvent/file/invoice` and actions `created/updated/completed/deleted`; payload carries `contractVersion, name, workspaceId, objectFamily, action, recordId, actor, timestamps, record`; `file` maps to the standard `attachment` object; a runtime `isCrossAppEventPayload` guard.

**Server** (`twenty-server/src/modules/cross-app-events`): `CrossAppLifecycleEventListener` hangs off `@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', …)`, a pure `mapDatabaseEventToCrossAppEvents` promotes task DONE updates to `completed`, gates `document` on a2e-documents and keeps `invoice` dormant behind a2e-accounting, and `CrossAppEventEmitterService` publishes on the single `cross_app_lifecycle` channel via the existing `WorkspaceEventEmitter`. Registered in `ModulesModule`. No app/recipe change needed — M9c recipe trigger names already equal the contract names.

**Checks green:** twenty-shared build + tsgo + 9 tests; twenty-server tsgo + 4 suites/19 tests (incl. a module-level integration spec); scoped oxlint/oxfmt clean; docs check pass; no `locales/**` churn. `Ready-to-tick: no` (reported `partial`): the DB-backed workflow-trigger integration spec and Tier-2 install/uninstall browser leg are listed under "Missing for tick" in `docs/plan/phases/phase-15-report.md`.

